# ---- Rust ----
# Compiled output
/target/
**/target/

# Backtrace / debug
*.pdb

# Cargo lock is kept for binaries/workspaces; uncomment if this is a library
# Cargo.lock

# rustc incremental / coverage
*.profraw
*.gcda
*.gcno

# proptest failure-persistence artifacts (auto-generated cache; not stable across runs)
**/*.proptest-regressions

# ---- Python ----
# Bytecode from the tracked helper scripts (scripts/stub-ollama.py is executed by
# `just verify-release-parity`, which regenerates this on every run).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- Editor / OS ----
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---- OSS / Cloud split (per `00-vision-and-principles.md` §6) ----
# The OSS workspace (this directory) is the public open-source runtime.
# The cloud-heavy trait impls live in `kx-cloud/` and are PRIVATE — they will
# be developed in their own (separate, private) git repository nested inside
# this subdirectory when P5.5 begins. Until then, the directory holds only a
# stubbed Cargo workspace as an architectural breadcrumb. NEVER commit
# kx-cloud contents to the OSS repo.
kx-cloud/

# ---- Internal docs (kept out of the public OSS repo) ----
# These live in the working tree but never land in `Kortecx/kortecx`. Wildcards
# auto-cover future additions so a new design / suggestion doc doesn't leak by
# accident.
/00-*.md
/01-*.md
/02-*.md
/03-*.md
/04-*.md
/05-*.md
/06-*.md
/07-*.md
/CLAUDE.md
# Local Claude Code agent state (plans, transcripts, settings) — never committed.
/.claude/
/docs/design/*.md
/docs/suggestions/*.md
# Internal analysis / feasibility reviews — kept out of tree.
/docs/analysis/
# Plan files are kept out of tree.
/docs/plans/
# Profiling/benchmark results are kept out of tree: the `just profile` HARNESS
# ships here, but the captured numbers are maintained separately. Ignored BEFORE
# any result file can exist so none is committed.
/docs/benchmarks/
# Internal warning/debug log — kept out of tree.
/WARNINGS.md

# Local code-review tooling runtime data (a throwaway review journal + catalog +
# content store); never a committed artifact.
/.kx-review-data/

# ---- Docker compose dev secrets ----
# Only the *.example templates are committed. A developer may copy them to the
# un-suffixed names below (or replace them) for local customization; the real
# secret files never land in git.
/deploy/secrets/kx_authtokens
/deploy/secrets/kx_token

# proptest failure-persistence DIRECTORIES (the pattern above only matched *.proptest-regressions files)
**/proptest-regressions/

# ---- Maintainer-local tooling — not part of the public runtime ----
# The public repo ships the runtime code plus scripts/install.sh. Other top-level
# dev/release helper scripts and their config are maintained out of tree; they are
# ignored here so they never land in a public checkout by accident. Any new
# scripts/*.sh is treated as local by default — a script that SHIPS needs an
# explicit exception below, or it silently never reaches a public checkout.
/shared-paths.toml
/feature-ledger.toml
/scripts/*.sh
!/scripts/install.sh
# The release workflow reads this to publish the CHANGELOG section as the release
# body, so it must be in the checkout the workflow runs against.
!/scripts/release-notes.sh
# The SINGLE owner of the release build+package body: release.yml calls it on a
# tag and `just verify-release-parity` calls it at PR time, so the packaging the
# gate proves is the packaging the tag runs. Untracked, both callers would run
# nothing — the registry-check incident shape, again.
!/scripts/package-release.sh
# The NL-authoring live proof and its detached supervisors. These SHIP: a proof that
# lives only on the machine that ran it is a claim, not evidence — anyone should be
# able to re-run the journey (propose -> approve -> registry, plus the refusal A/B)
# against their own served model and get the same verdict. The supervisors carry the
# lease discipline (per-session ports, `ollama stop` between engine arms) that a
# hand-run sequence gets wrong.
!/scripts/proof-nl-authoring.sh
!/scripts/run-live-proof.sh
!/scripts/run-bench-recapture.sh
!/scripts/run-live-sweep.sh
# `just ci` and a bare `clippy --lib` both miss a non-default feature's module AND
# its tests, so each feature needs its own `--all-targets` clippy + `test` pair. That
# is a standing gap in the gate, and a runner that encodes it is worth more than a
# note somebody has to remember at the end of a long session.
!/scripts/run-feature-gates.sh
# A member of `just ci`. It was untracked here, so the recipe printed "skipped" and
# returned 0 in every checkout — the ignore file was the reason the gate never ran.
!/scripts/registry-check.sh
# The Docker channel's in-container gate. Same shape as registry-check above, and it
# already happened: the script was removed, the recipe reported "skipped", and the CI
# job stayed green while executing nothing. `gitignore_guard` asserts both that this
# line exists AND that the file is tracked, so the pair cannot come apart again.
!/scripts/docker-smoke.sh
/justfile.private

# The packed SDK the gateway embeds and serves as an installable package — a BUILD
# artifact of `just console-dist`, regenerated from bindings/typescript, never committed.
bindings/typescript/kortecx-sdk.tgz

# SQLite sidecars beside the FROZEN state-dir fixtures. Opening a WAL-mode database
# creates `-wal`/`-shm` even for a read-only connection, so running the frozen-state-dir
# tests leaves them in the fixture tree. They are not part of the captured truth, and a
# `git add -A` that swept them in would corrupt the very artifact the fixtures preserve.
crates/kx-runtime/tests/fixtures/state-dirs/**/*.db-wal
crates/kx-runtime/tests/fixtures/state-dirs/**/*.db-shm
crates/kx-runtime/tests/fixtures/state-dirs/**/*.db-journal

# Node dependency and cache trees, at ANY depth. The per-package ignores covered
# `ui/`, `bindings/typescript/` and `docs/site/`, but nothing covered the repository
# ROOT — so a test runner invoked from the root rather than from `ui/` created a
# top-level `node_modules/` whose vitest cache was tracked, and committed.
node_modules/
.vite/
